// Win32 resource script for the engine executable.
//
// The shipped binary carries a GROUP_ICON whose resource name is the string
// IDI_WIN_FAICON (rva 0x00E8A2E0, nine images: 16/32/48/256 px at 4, 8 and 32
// bpp). It is a *named* resource, not a numeric id, which is what an .rc line
// produces when the symbol on the left is not #defined - so the original
// script said the same thing this one does.
//
// WSupComFrame's constructor (0x008CD8C0) asks for exactly this name at
// 0x008CD9F2, via wxIcon(L"IDI_WIN_FAICON", wxBITMAP_TYPE_ICO_RESOURCE), and
// wxICOResourceHandler::Load (0x009ABE80) resolves it with
// LoadIconW(wxGetInstance(), name). Without this script that lookup returns
// null, the frame has no icon, and Windows falls back to the generic default
// in the caption bar and the taskbar.
//
// faicon.ico was rebuilt from that GROUP_ICON and its nine ICON resources.
IDI_WIN_FAICON ICON "res/faicon.ico"
